# Seed the relocalization search with an initial pose guess.
#
# Backed by three device custom parameters (see the official Relocalization Guide):
#   "init_pos"                 float[7] = [x, y, z, qx, qy, qz, qw]   (metres, normalised quat)
#   "init_pose_search_radius"  float    metres, recommended <= 10
#   "init_pose_max_rot_deg"    float    degrees, <= 180
#
# TIMING CONTRACT (this is the part that bites people):
#   The device only consumes init_pos when the algorithm (re)starts, i.e. before
#   lidar_start_stream(). Calling this service while streaming stores the value on
#   the device but does NOT trigger a new relocalization attempt.
#     - applied_immediately == false  -> value staged; call SwitchMode (or restart
#                                        the driver) to make the algorithm use it.
#     - applied_immediately == true   -> the stream was not running, so the next
#                                        start will consume it directly.
#
# The pose is expressed in the MAP frame (the world frame at the time the map was
# built). This service accepts RViz's "2D Pose Estimate" message type directly, so
# /initialpose can be bridged to it with a one-line relay.

geometry_msgs/PoseWithCovarianceStamped pose

float32 search_radius_m 0.0       # <= 0 -> leave the device parameter unchanged
float32 max_rot_deg 0.0           # <= 0 -> leave the device parameter unchanged
---
bool success
int32 rc                          # 0 ok; -100 device not open; -2 file transfer busy
bool applied_immediately
string message
